% DOI POLICY, and why this file deliberately does NOT mirror these into note.
%
% The three authored entries below now carry a Zenodo DOI (10.5281/zenodo.*).
% The earlier instruction here was to mirror a filled doi into note as well,
% because IEEEtran.bst never prints the doi field. That mirroring is now
% withheld on purpose: main.pdf shipped to Zenodo as v1 and its bytes are
% frozen at 85c22506..., so a note that prints a DOI would describe a PDF
% that does not exist. Keeping the identifier in the machine-readable field
% only means the sources still typeset the archived bytes, while tools can
% still resolve the DOI. If a future revision wants the DOI visible in print,
% that is a v2 recompile -- not a silent edit here.
%
% Note also that these DOIs are registered with DataCite, not CrossRef.
% A resolver that only knows CrossRef will 404 on them and must not be read as
% evidence of a bad identifier; doi.org/DataCite resolves all three.

@software{liaozhizhi2026sidecar,
